# FINAL TAKEAWAY

> **A real-life cyberattack simulation is an authorized, controlled exercise that reproduces selected adversary behaviors to evaluate prevention, detection, response, and recovery capabilities. The ultimate goal is to discover security gaps and improve the organization's defenses—not to cause damage.**